ext4 read: split cache hits from physical waits

lwext4's mount lock spans every public operation and every block wait. Keep
writes, journal state and lifecycle exclusive, but give file reads a shared
side. Protect cache metadata briefly and serialize fills through the physical
device lane; a peer rechecks the completed buffer instead of reading twice.

Covered by sw/userspace/storage's `make ext4-test`, `make ext4-sanitize`, and
`make ext4-tsan`. The controlled backend holds A in a cold read, requires warm
B to finish without I/O, and requires a second cold A to reuse the first fill.

